WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.291
The first couple of Thor movies lacked a little
something — at least, when compared to the

00:00:04.291 --> 00:00:07.029
likes of Iron Man and Captain America: The
Winter Soldier.

00:00:07.029 --> 00:00:11.130
That all changed when director Taika Waititi
came onboard to helm Thor: Ragnarok, the third

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:14.690
installment of the series, and a film that
completely changed what was possible within

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:16.510
the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:19.750
Waititi will be coming back for the sequel
— Thor: Love and Thunder — and based on

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:23.599
everything we know about the film so far,
he's going to take these heroes in even wilder

00:00:23.599 --> 00:00:25.130
directions than before.

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:28.770
In addition to having the Guardians of the
Galaxy play a role, Jane Foster, played by

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:33.360
Natalie Portman, is returning to the superhero
franchise after being absent from Ragnarok.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:37.130
This time around, though, she's not just playing
a love interest: She's donning the title of

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:41.370
Mighty Thor herself, and by the looks of an
exclusive behind-the-scenes photo that Looper

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:45.050
obtained from BACKGRID – she's taking the
part very seriously.

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:49.040
But preparing for her big superhero role by
never skipping arm day shouldn't come as a

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:51.400
surprise to anyone familiar with Portman's
career.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:55.940
The Academy Award winner has always gone above
and beyond to reflect the characters she plays.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:59.460
Most famously, she actually shaved her head
when her character had to do the same in V

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:03.880
for Vendetta, but even that pales in comparison
to what she had to do for Black Swan.

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:08.370
Ballerinas naturally have to be in exceptional
physical condition to dance the way they do,

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:12.540
and to properly showcase the art form, Portman
reportedly trained six days a week for up

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:15.620
to eight hours a day so that she could really
dance like a ballerina.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:19.781
Her training regimen there was obviously different
from what she's doing to become Thor, but

00:01:19.781 --> 00:01:23.630
it's clear she has the perseverance to adhere
to any workout schedule.

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:27.750
Even when Natalie Portman isn't necessarily
training for a role, she knows how to stay

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:28.750
in shape.

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:32.140
In a 2019 interview with Women's Health, the
megastar discussed how she keeps up her strength

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:33.810
even when her schedule gets hectic.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:35.170
As she described it,

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:36.910
"I run maybe three times a week.

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:40.409
When I'm running for a full hour... it feels
a little like meditation to me."

00:01:40.409 --> 00:01:44.670
Later, she discusses how she's a fan of a
style of exercise known as gyrotonics, which

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:48.490
essentially consists of movements you'd find
with Tai Chi, yoga, gymnastics, and other

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:51.360
disciplines all wrapped into one convenient
package.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:55.560
Ultimately, it sounds like she keeps an open
mind and exercises in whatever manner is most

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:57.210
convenient in the moment, stating,

00:01:57.210 --> 00:02:01.060
"I used to do Ashtanga, but now, I'll just
get there and I'll try anything."

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:05.420
Considering the results, we'd say this routine
has definitely worked well for her — and

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:08.360
what Portman has shared in public about her
training so far sounds brutal.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:12.600
She went on The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy
Fallon to offer an update on Thor: Love and

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:16.230
Thunder, and while shooting hadn't started
at the time, Portman was already being put

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:17.230
through the wringer.

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:21.130
And from the sound of things, she wasn't exactly
in the best place mentally to start an intense

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:22.130
regimen.

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:23.130
She told Fallon,

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:27.280
"I'm trying, I've had like, months of like,
pandemic, you know, eating baked goods and,

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.400
like lying in bed, and feeling sorry for myself."

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:36.380
"I'm like, super tired after working out,
and during, and dreading before."

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:40.650
Around that same time, she also stopped by
Watch What Happens Live With Andy Cohen where

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:44.600
she was asked if she had to be on a workout
plan similar to her co-star Chris Hemsworth.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:47.720
She said that she was, and she wasn't taking
to it very easily.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:50.750
"Yes, I am training, and I'm in so much pain.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:52.690
Like, I'm not good at this."

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:56.819
Maddy Black, formerly a Crossfit coach with
Vogue Fitness, offered some of her insight

00:02:56.819 --> 00:03:00.819
into how Portman could accomplish such gains
in an interview with Ahlan Live.

00:03:00.819 --> 00:03:01.819
She said,

00:03:01.819 --> 00:03:05.400
"Natalie will be carrying out lots of compound
weightlifting movements such as squatting,

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:06.630
pressing and pulling.

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:10.070
In order to remain 'lean' for the role, she
will be implementing some high intensity interval

00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:11.510
training into her weekly routine."

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:15.890
She goes on to explain how she would go about
designing an exercise regimen for someone

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:20.130
wanting the kind of arms Jane Foster's Thor
has in the comics, declaring,

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:24.120
"Weightlifting would form the foundation base
whilst functional training would develop skills,

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.220
improve flexibility and enhance endurance."

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:30.599
We may not know exactly how heavy her weights
are, but it's definitely clear she's been

00:03:30.599 --> 00:03:32.540
pumping iron in one way or another.

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:36.459
We didn't think there was any way Portman
could look more intimidating than in her "Natalie

00:03:36.459 --> 00:03:40.260
Raps" video, but judging from those guns,
she just proved us wrong.

